/**
 * @defgroup StMuDSTEZTREE StMuDSTMaker/EZTREE — Raw Data Blobs
 * @brief Lightweight raw-data format stored alongside the MuDST for trigger and EMC monitoring.
 * @details
 * The EZTREE package provides a set of compact "blob" classes that preserve
 * the unprocessed trigger structure and EEMC (Endcap EMC) ADC crate buffers
 * verbatim inside the MuDST ROOT file.  Each blob is registered as a separate
 * TTree branch alongside the standard MuDST branches.
 *
 * The bridge class StMuEzTree is called once per event by StMuDstMaker.  It
 * copies data from StEvent into heap-allocated Ezt* objects:
 *
 *   - EztEventHeader  — run/event number, trigger token, timestamps
 *   - EztTrigBlob     — full raw trigger C-struct plus a version byte
 *   - EztFpdBlob      — raw Forward Pion Detector SMD data
 *   - EztEmcRawData   — raw EEMC tower crate buffers (crates 0–5)
 *   - EztEmcRawData   — raw EEMC SMD crate buffers   (crates 6–N)
 *
 * When reading back, StTriggerDataMother inspects the version byte in
 * EztTrigBlob and instantiates the appropriate year-specific StTriggerData20xx
 * object, providing a single year-transparent interface for trigger decoding.
 *
 * EZT branches may be enabled or disabled individually at read time via
 * StMuDstMaker::SetStatus("Ezt*", 0/1).
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @class StMuEzTree
 * @brief Bridge class that copies raw data from StEvent into Ezt* blob objects.
 *
 * StMuEzTree is instantiated by StMuDstMaker and its copy methods are called
 * once per event.  The returned objects are stored as MuDST TTree branches.
 *
 * The constant mxETowCrate = 6 defines the boundary between the EEMC tower
 * crate range (indices 0–5) and the EEMC SMD crate range (indices 6–N) within
 * the source StEmcRawData object.
 */

/**
 * @class EztEventHeader
 * @brief Minimal event header stored in the EZT branch.
 *
 * Holds the run number, event number, trigger token (from StL0Trigger), the
 * event Unix timestamp, the DST-production Unix timestamp, a status word, and
 * a variable-length comment string.  The token must match the token embedded
 * inside the trigger and EMC crate headers; a mismatch indicates data
 * corruption.
 */

/**
 * @class EztTrigBlob
 * @brief Container for the full raw STAR trigger data structure.
 *
 * Stores the raw trigger C-struct as a TArrayC (trgd), an auxiliary trigger-ID
 * bank (trgid, reserved for future use), and a one-byte version code that
 * identifies the year-specific layout of the C-struct.  The version byte is
 * used by StTriggerDataMother to select the correct StTriggerData20xx decoder.
 */

/**
 * @class EztFpdBlob
 * @brief Container for raw Forward Pion Detector data.
 *
 * Stores raw FPD SMD words in a TArrayS (smd).  At the time of initial
 * development, only placeholder data was written; a production-quality
 * implementation reading from StEvent::fpdCollection() was planned.
 */

/**
 * @class EztEmcRawData
 * @brief Raw EEMC ADC crate buffers for one group of crates (ETOW or ESMD).
 *
 * Holds up to MAXEMCDATABANK = 60 crate blocks.  Each block contains a
 * 4-word header (TArrayS mHeader) and a variable-length payload (TArrayS
 * mData).  A per-block corruption status word (mCorrupt, default 0xffff) is
 * set to 0 only after a successful header-validation call.
 *
 * Header word layout (indices WRDCNT=0, ERRFLG=1, TOKEN=2, CRATE=3):
 *   - bits [11:0] of word 0: length count
 *   - bits [11:0] of word 1: error flags
 *   - bits [11:0] of word 2: trigger token
 *   - bits  [7:0] of word 3: crate ID
 *   - bits [11:8] of word 3: trigger command
 *
 * Static accessor methods (getToken, getCrateID, etc.) operate on a raw
 * header pointer and can be called without a class instance.
 *
 * Two separate EztEmcRawData objects are stored per event: one for the six
 * ETOW crates (produced by StMuEzTree::copyETow) and one for the ESMD crates
 * (produced by StMuEzTree::copyESmd).
 */

/**
 * @class StTriggerDataMother
 * @brief Year-transparent wrapper for decoding a persisted EztTrigBlob.
 *
 * Inherits from StTriggerData and delegates all virtual calls to an internal
 * fCurrent pointer.  The constructor reads the version byte from the supplied
 * EztTrigBlob and constructs the matching year-specific decoder:
 *   - 0x20 → StTriggerData2003
 *   - 0x21 → StTriggerData2004
 *   - 0x22 → StTriggerData2005
 *
 * Exposes DSM intermediate-level accessors: getDsm0_EEMC, getDsm1_EEMC,
 * getDsm2_EMC, getDsm3.  The destructor deletes fCurrent.
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
